Fix `Gib` -> `Gio` typo in cinnamon-screensaver's PAM helper client.

`AuthClient.message_to_child()` wraps `self.in_pipe.flush(None)` in a
`except GLib.Error` handler, but that handler dereferences `Gib.IOErrorEnum`.
`Gib` is not defined anywhere in the module -- `Gio` is imported at the top --
so any non-cancelled GLib.Error raised by flush() raises `NameError: name 'Gib'
is not defined` from inside the error handler instead of being reported. That
leaves the PAM helper's stdin pipe in the state the surrounding cleanup path
was meant to handle.

Reproduced against cinnamon-screensaver 6.6.1+zena: driving message_to_child()
with an in_pipe whose flush() raises Gio.IOErrorEnum.BROKEN_PIPE lets
`NameError: name 'Gib' is not defined` escape the call.

Reported upstream: https://github.com/linuxmint/cinnamon-screensaver/issues/512
(open 2026-08-23; still present in upstream master at time of writing).

This is unrelated to the exit-time `Error in sys.excepthook` burst documented
in docs/cinnamon-screensaver-errors.md -- that code path runs synchronously
from `on_unlock_clicked`, not during finalization.

Apply with patches/apply-cinnamon-screensaver-gib-patch.sh (which diverts the
package-owned file so `apt upgrade` does not silently revert this).

--- a/pamhelper/authClient.py
+++ b/pamhelper/authClient.py
@@ -152,7 +152,7 @@
 
             self.in_pipe.flush(None)
         except GLib.Error as e:
-            if e.code != Gib.IOErrorEnum.CANCELLED:
+            if e.code != Gio.IOErrorEnum.CANCELLED:
                 print("Error writing to pam helper: %s" % e.message)
 
     def message_from_child(self, pipe, res):
